(5983513, 875016, 115345, '<td valign="top">6 from me.  I think the intent was good, for me the eye/hand positioning with the thumb intruding on the eye didn''t work.  Doing this kind of shot is not easy I understand but in the end I tend to judge on how the image strikes me irrespective of the difficulty getting the shot and I think a slightly different placement of the eye would have pushed more of my buttons.  That is just me though.</td>', '6 from me.  I think the intent was good, for me the eye/hand positioning with the thumb intruding on the eye didn''t work.  Doing this kind of shot is not easy I understand but in the end I tend to judge on how the image strikes me irrespective of the difficulty getting the shot and I think a slightly different placement of the eye would have pushed more of my buttons.  That is just me though.', '2010-05-01 22:04:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5983522, 874371, 115345, '<td valign="top">sorry had to give a 6.  Everyone judges differently but for me the image demonstrates double exposure well but the double exposure doesn''t actually enhance the impact of the image (to me).  To me it says - "here is a really clean image of a flower and here it is upside down to show a technique"... and I think - "does doing that really make the photo better?"   I know you are caught between a rock and a hard place... on this site some people tend to judge highly on meeting the challenge (hopefully they will score you highly to balance me) and you have met it well and some judge more on the overall impact.  I lean a lot on the impact side - sorry it didn''t do the impact (for me).  If you could have managed to have something different about the 2 parts then that probably would have pushed it higher in my eyes.<br/> <br/>NB that is just me - no criticism of technique (is well done) just a long winded comment how it struck me as an individual.</td>', 'sorry had to give a 6.  Everyone judges differently but for me the image demonstrates double exposure well but the double exposure doesn''t actually enhance the impact of the image (to me).  To me it says - "here is a really clean image of a flower and here it is upside down to show a technique"... and I think - "does doing that really make the photo better?"   I know you are caught between a rock and a hard place... on this site some people tend to judge highly on meeting the challenge (hopefully they will score you highly to balance me) and you have met it well and some judge more on the overall impact.  I lean a lot on the impact side - sorry it didn''t do the impact (for me).  If you could have managed to have something different about the 2 parts then that probably would have pushed it higher in my eyes. NB that is just me - no criticism of technique (is well done) just a long winded comment how it struck me as an individual.', '2010-05-01 22:14:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5983532, 875231, 115345, '<td valign="top">The double exposure is well done and the composition shows a clear intent tend to use the technique to achieve a point.  If you could have managed to get the inner child more centered I would have scored it highly - as it is the balance feels wrong so I have had to give it a 6 - sorry.  I understand that getting this short of shot is difficult (doubt I could do it) but I tend to judge more on the overall impact of an image - this one had potential but didn''t quite get there (for me - others will see it differently).</td>', 'The double exposure is well done and the composition shows a clear intent tend to use the technique to achieve a point.  If you could have managed to get the inner child more centered I would have scored it highly - as it is the balance feels wrong so I have had to give it a 6 - sorry.  I understand that getting this short of shot is difficult (doubt I could do it) but I tend to judge more on the overall impact of an image - this one had potential but didn''t quite get there (for me - others will see it differently).', '2010-05-01 22:19:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984418, 874935, 86218, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done. Would score this higher and want more detail/visual eye. Had difficulty really seeing the eye but once you know its easy. 7</td>', 'Very nicely done. Would score this higher and want more detail/visual eye. Had difficulty really seeing the eye but once you know its easy. 7', '2010-05-02 12:51:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984444, 874523, 60046, '<td valign="top">Simple yet effective.</td>', 'Simple yet effective.', '2010-05-02 13:21:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5984492, 875189, 96881, '<td valign="top">A really good idea here, but I feel the execution lets it down a bit.  I note you have exposed the image for the surrounds, and presume you had a long exposure that allowed you to move positions.  The negative that always comes with that method is the ghosting that occurs, and here the bright (and busy) background showing through does effect the overall result.<br/>The use of flash in these cases (flash, change position, flash again) usually gives better results, as does being on a dark background so that there is less effect on your image.<br/>But a great try at it.<br/>Also, I am sure others have noticed, the image is tilted.........</td>', 'A really good idea here, but I feel the execution lets it down a bit.  I note you have exposed the image for the surrounds, and presume you had a long exposure that allowed you to move positions.  The negative that always comes with that method is the ghosting that occurs, and here the bright (and busy) background showing through does effect the overall result.The use of flash in these cases (flash, change position, flash again) usually gives better results, as does being on a dark background so that there is less effect on your image.But a great try at it.Also, I am sure others have noticed, the image is tilted.........', '2010-05-02 14:04:48.000000', NULL, 1),
