(5991516, 875079, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like the creases, too.</td>', 'I like the creases, too.', '2010-05-05 03:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991523, 874330, 114233, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for the wonderful comments. I am very happy to finish in top 10 seeing it is my highest finish... but I was sectretly hoping for a higher placing :-) Would really love the people that gave me votes of 1-4 to comment so I can see why they gave low scores and try to improve.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for the wonderful comments. I am very happy to finish in top 10 seeing it is my highest finish... but I was sectretly hoping for a higher placing :-) Would really love the people that gave me votes of 1-4 to comment so I can see why they gave low scores and try to improve.', '2010-05-05 03:20:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991533, 874599, 16520, '<td valign="top">Great job Richard to bad we were''nt first and second..</td>', 'Great job Richard to bad we were''nt first and second..', '2010-05-05 03:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991547, 874793, 68413, '<td valign="top">Brilliant Jason. Thanks for the heads up on the PP. Congratulations on another well deserved blue ribbon.</td>', 'Brilliant Jason. Thanks for the heads up on the PP. Congratulations on another well deserved blue ribbon.', '2010-05-05 03:35:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991554, 874793, 103048, '<td valign="top">This is awesome. Great work!</td>', 'This is awesome. Great work!', '2010-05-05 03:39:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991555, 874935, 41337, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this didn''t fare better.</td>', 'I''m surprised this didn''t fare better.', '2010-05-05 03:40:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991558, 874330, 106910, '<td valign="top">Honestly - they probably just didn''t like the content of the photo. I think it''s marvelous and well executed. Grats on your top 10 finish!</td>', 'Honestly - they probably just didn''t like the content of the photo. I think it''s marvelous and well executed. Grats on your top 10 finish!', '2010-05-05 03:41:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991559, 875184, 68413, '<td valign="top">Hey Shannon, I would have put money on this one taking out a ribbon and from my POV ''the blue''. 5 ones - I actually don''t believe it - bloody morons. Congrats on the top 5 anyway. It''s still a brilliant image.</td>', 'Hey Shannon, I would have put money on this one taking out a ribbon and from my POV ''the blue''. 5 ones - I actually don''t believe it - bloody morons. Congrats on the top 5 anyway. It''s still a brilliant image.', '2010-05-05 03:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991561, 874793, 23430, '<td valign="top">Mate, how good is that.<br/>I wouldn''t have thought of that or carried it out like you have in a million years.<br/>Very well done and congrats.</td>', 'Mate, how good is that.I wouldn''t have thought of that or carried it out like you have in a million years.Very well done and congrats.', '2010-05-05 03:43:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991573, 874316, 114969, '<td valign="top">I agree with Brent here, the result is great, doing this with basic editing is an absolute nightmare. Fantastic work!</td>', 'I agree with Brent here, the result is great, doing this with basic editing is an absolute nightmare. Fantastic work!', '2010-05-05 03:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991599, 874376, 105130, '<td valign="top">Great result man, and a big ''Booooooo'' to all the people claiming it''s more than two exposures. For all they know, you could have an identical twin! Way to go.</td>', 'Great result man, and a big ''Booooooo'' to all the people claiming it''s more than two exposures. For all they know, you could have an identical twin! Way to go.', '2010-05-05 04:25:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991614, 873346, 116055, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments! there are question regarding "where is the double exposure". from what i understood with the rules and theme, this idea is what i came up with due to lack of double exposure feature in my cam.<br/> <br/>just put it this way. first exposure (long exposure) is for the light trail, second one is for the face coming from an off camera flash. although technically my camera only exposed/clicked once. the exposure i had in mind was for two main element on the photo.<br/> <br/>just thinking out loud : )<br/> <br/>thanks for the votes!</td>', 'thanks for the comments! there are question regarding "where is the double exposure". from what i understood with the rules and theme, this idea is what i came up with due to lack of double exposure feature in my cam. just put it this way. first exposure (long exposure) is for the light trail, second one is for the face coming from an off camera flash. although technically my camera only exposed/clicked once. the exposure i had in mind was for two main element on the photo. just thinking out loud : ) thanks for the votes!', '2010-05-05 04:57:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5991617, 873346, 116055, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by klkitchens:</b></div><hr/><i> appears to be slow shutter, not double exposure </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>it is indeed a slow shutter but only for the light trails. an off camera was used for the the face.</td>', 'Originally posted by klkitchens: appears to be slow shutter, not double exposure   it is indeed a slow shutter but only for the light trails. an off camera was used for the the face.', '2010-05-05 04:59:18.000000', NULL, 0),
