(5993692, 874877, 22734, '<td valign="top">Good execution and a pleasant eyeful.</td>', 'Good execution and a pleasant eyeful.', '2010-05-06 02:51:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5993699, 874834, 22734, '<td valign="top">Love the smoke. A good concept with pleasing colors. However, this is very difficult shot to accomplish in a long exposure because the flame easily over exposes. There is a way to do it, but not very practical. I have an old 8 x 10 view camera with a shutter. You remove the lens and place your gear behind the shutter. Now, you can control the exposure on the candle light.</td>', 'Love the smoke. A good concept with pleasing colors. However, this is very difficult shot to accomplish in a long exposure because the flame easily over exposes. There is a way to do it, but not very practical. I have an old 8 x 10 view camera with a shutter. You remove the lens and place your gear behind the shutter. Now, you can control the exposure on the candle light.', '2010-05-06 03:04:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5993701, 875202, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very good concept. Avoid the white because it eliminates anything that comes across it. A darker shirt would have allowed a better completion of the circular center light curve. However, the image has good visual impact and your show great promise. Keep at it.</td>', 'A very good concept. Avoid the white because it eliminates anything that comes across it. A darker shirt would have allowed a better completion of the circular center light curve. However, the image has good visual impact and your show great promise. Keep at it.', '2010-05-06 03:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5993778, 874330, 114233, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SaraR:</b></div><hr/><i> I was one of your 7s - thought it technically very good, although it didn''t resonate as much with me as a final image.  I''m curious as to how you got the hands to disappear entirely behind the teeth, rather than having some ghosting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is quite simple really. I had my palms facing straight up (as though I was pushing on the ceiling). It also helped that the flash was fired by hand from a low position (see the knee shadow)so the palms were almost perfectly black. I just happened to get get good positioning after about 40 shots... the other shots overlapped badly or were no where near the teeth. Hope that clears up a few issues.</td>', 'Originally posted by SaraR: I was one of your 7s - thought it technically very good, although it didn''t resonate as much with me as a final image.  I''m curious as to how you got the hands to disappear entirely behind the teeth, rather than having some ghosting.   It is quite simple really. I had my palms facing straight up (as though I was pushing on the ceiling). It also helped that the flash was fired by hand from a low position (see the knee shadow)so the palms were almost perfectly black. I just happened to get get good positioning after about 40 shots... the other shots overlapped badly or were no where near the teeth. Hope that clears up a few issues.', '2010-05-06 04:28:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5994021, 875221, 99548, '<td valign="top">This shot is the greatest idea of this challange. Maybe you did use wine instead of blue water, you could do better. Blue ribbon goes to you, from my heart ofcourse =).</td>', 'This shot is the greatest idea of this challange. Maybe you did use wine instead of blue water, you could do better. Blue ribbon goes to you, from my heart ofcourse =).', '2010-05-06 07:47:07.000000', NULL, 0),
