(5994511, 875184, 73564, '<td valign="top">Every time I see this picture... it reminds me of this photo I did....<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=878731" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70000-74999/73564/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_878731.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70000-74999/73564/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_878731.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/70000-74999/73564/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_878731.jpg"/></a> The quality isnt so hot, but it still makes me laugh.</td>', 'Every time I see this picture... it reminds me of this photo I did.... The quality isnt so hot, but it still makes me laugh.', '2010-05-06 16:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5994529, 874330, 67258, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Silent-Shooter:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SaraR:</b></div><hr/><i> I was one of your 7s - thought it technically very good, although it didn''t resonate as much with me as a final image.  I''m curious as to how you got the hands to disappear entirely behind the teeth, rather than having some ghosting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is quite simple really. I had my palms facing straight up (as though I was pushing on the ceiling). It also helped that the flash was fired by hand from a low position (see the knee shadow)so the palms were almost perfectly black. I just happened to get get good positioning after about 40 shots... the other shots overlapped badly or were no where near the teeth. Hope that clears up a few issues. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That makes sense.  An intriguing shot.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Silent-Shooter: Originally posted by SaraR: I was one of your 7s - thought it technically very good, although it didn''t resonate as much with me as a final image.  I''m curious as to how you got the hands to disappear entirely behind the teeth, rather than having some ghosting.   It is quite simple really. I had my palms facing straight up (as though I was pushing on the ceiling). It also helped that the flash was fired by hand from a low position (see the knee shadow)so the palms were almost perfectly black. I just happened to get get good positioning after about 40 shots... the other shots overlapped badly or were no where near the teeth. Hope that clears up a few issues.   That makes sense.  An intriguing shot.', '2010-05-06 17:13:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5994746, 874731, 98339, '<td valign="top">I really liked this one...it was one of my higher scores...well done with the clarity and focus...not an easy thing to do was it....</td>', 'I really liked this one...it was one of my higher scores...well done with the clarity and focus...not an easy thing to do was it....', '2010-05-06 20:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
